# LifecycleCompass — D-001 Directive (Repo Init, Current State, Guardrails, Verification)

**Issued**: 2026-08-22
**Status**: Consolidated directive — repo init + scope + current build state + what's not done + guardrails + verification, following the same single-directive pattern used for CyberCompass/eIFUCompass/ClinicalCompass/DocCompass.
**Source artifact**: `lifecyclecompass.html`, marker `v2.0.0-rc3 · build 2026-08-22`
**Do not split this into D-001/D-002.** Everything the implementor needs to start is here.

---

## §0 — Repo Init

LifecycleCompass has no repo yet — this is the first directive for this tool.

- **Remote**: `git@github.com:rajeevyadav/lifecyclecompass.git` (propose — confirm before first push; matches sibling naming: cybercompass, eifucompass)
- **Local working folder**: `D:\G-Drive\RY-DEV\LifecycleCompass` (propose — confirm; matches sibling folder pattern)
- **Commit authorship**: ALL commits authored solely as `Rajeev Yadav <rajeevyadav@gmail.com>` — no other identity permitted, no exceptions. Set local-only git identity in this repo, same as CyberCompass.
- **First push (R-001 scope)**: init repo, add `lifecyclecompass.html` as the initial commit, README stub, branch protection (force-push/deletion off; PR-required off, matching CyberCompass's chosen setting), version marker stamped to the actual first commit hash.
- **Signed commits**: deferred, same status as the other repos currently.
- **STRICT: human-committer-only policy — see §5a. This is non-negotiable and applies from the very first commit.**

---

## §1 — Scope (unchanged from spec v0.1/v2.0)

LifecycleCompass maps, assesses, and traces the nested development and lifecycle processes of AI-enabled medical devices — AI Data Management Lifecycle → AI Development Lifecycle → Software Development Lifecycle → Software System Lifecycle → Software System with Hardware → Medical Device at Product Level (ISO 13485 + emerging AI-MS). Decision-support only, not conformity assessment. Same family philosophy as every Compass tool: 100% deterministic, human-authored rules, no AI in the assessment logic, fully offline.

**Jurisdiction scope: EU MDR + FDA only** — stated explicitly in the tool's §0 tab, not silent. UK/Health Canada/other jurisdictions are out of scope.

---

## §2 — Design System (confirmed, do not re-litigate)

- Light/dark toggle, indigo/violet accent `#5b47e0` — deliberately distinct from every sibling (teal used by RegCompass/eIFUCompass/ClinicalCompass; orange/dark used by CyberCompass; navy/coral-red by DocCompass)
- Rounded corners (10px), soft shadows, gradient header
- This went through two rejected experiments (OfferPath cream/serif look, Palantir dark/sharp/mono look) before landing back on this — **do not propose either of those directions again without being asked.**
- Print stylesheet exists (reveals all tabs, strips nav/buttons for PDF export)
- Accessibility pass done: focus-visible outlines, `role="tab"`/`aria-selected`, aria-labels on icon-only controls — not independently audited for WCAG contrast ratios (see §6)

