## §3 — What Has Been Built (current state, port must preserve all of this)

14 tabs, all functional, not stubbed:

| # | Tab | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | Scope & Limitations | Full intended-use/target-users/limitations/residual-risk statement (spec §2 content), rule-provenance tag legend, version history |
| 1 | Profiler | Multi-axis device/AI profile — base class, FDA pathway, AI presence, **model type (traditional/LLM-genAI)**, **planned modification strategy**, SOUP flag, hardware, software class, connectivity, data characteristics, clinical pathway, **AI Act applicability/tier/Art.6 route**, **assessment date**, **device intended use (free text — feeds Gate 1)** |
| 2 | Nested Lifecycle | SVG diagram redrawn from the reference image (dims by profile) + 6 rings with purpose/failure-mode text and evidence-state criteria |
| 3 | SOUP & Foundation Models | Ownership/control-based checklist (not simple binary SOUP classification) — source, freeze-ability, supplier notification, anomaly list |
| 4 | Standards Library | 16 entries, live-filtered by profile, **date-staleness flagging** (>90 days since last-verified relative to assessment date), LLM/genAI exclusion flag on ISO/TS 24971-2, supporting refs (ISO/IEC 5338/23894/42005) clearly separated as non-scored |
| 5 | Interfaces & Traceability | 6 named hand-offs, controlled/partial/gap states |
| 6 | QMS / AI-MS Overlay | ISO 13485 + AI-MS (ISO/IEC 42001, EN 18286) scope checklist |
| 6b | Cybersecurity Cross-Link | 6 lifecycle-mapped checkpoints, points to CyberCompass for depth |
| 6c | Clinical Evidence Cross-Link | 5 lifecycle-mapped checkpoints, points to ClinicalCompass for depth |
| 6d | **EU AI Act Overlay** | Obligation-group → existing-control mapping table + applicability/tier/Art.6 routing display |
| 6e | **Change & Postmarket Control** | 7 sub-areas (performance monitoring, drift, change triggers, retraining, rollback, PMS/CAPA, retirement) + **PCCP status panel** driven independently by AI presence AND planned modification strategy |
| 7 | Readiness & Report | **4-dimension readiness dashboard** (Lifecycle Completeness / Evidence Strength / Interface Coherence / Change Readiness) + **8 non-compensatory critical gates** + Green/Amber/Red/Grey banner + CSV + **JSON export** |
| — | Compass Family | Cross-links to sibling tools |
| — | Glossary | 31 plain-language term definitions |

**Core architecture, must survive the port exactly as-is:**

- **Evidence-state model** (`EVIDENCE_STATES` const, 7 states: not_assessed/evidence/partial/gap/undetermined/accepted/na) replaced binary checkboxes everywhere. `evRow()` is the shared renderer for every criterion row.
- **Rule-provenance tags**: every one of the 87 criteria is prefixed `[REG|STD|GUID|DRAFT|ED·optional-ref]` and parsed by `evRow()` into a colored badge. **Do not strip or "clean up" these prefixes during port** — they are load-bearing, not decoration. Where a criterion is tagged `ED`, that is a deliberate, honest statement that no single normative citation exists for it — do not "fix" this by inventing a citation.
- **Non-compensatory critical gates** (`CRITICAL_GATES` const, 8 gates, `stateToGate()` helper): a single failed gate forces the overall readiness to RED regardless of how high the 4 dimension scores read. **This is the single most important piece of the whole redesign — verified by test to actually work (all-evidence-except-one-empty-field still produces RED). Do not let this get "simplified" into a weighted average during port; that would silently reintroduce the exact flaw the P0 review identified.**
- **PCCP logic**: driven by `pccpStatus()`, combining AI presence AND planned modification strategy as independent axes — not AI type alone. This was the review's #1 flagged defect in the previous architecture; the fix must survive.

**Bugs found and fixed during this build — do not let any of these regress on port:**
1. Ring criteria (SOUP extra item, PCCP item) previously didn't re-render on profile change — fixed by calling all `renderX()` functions inside `applyProfile()`.
2. Hardcoded hex colors (`#0d7377`) inside the SVG diagram didn't respond to theme/accent changes — fixed by switching to `var(--teal)`.
3. Duplicate SOUP checklist (same criterion appeared in both §2 swdev ring and §3) — reconciled to a single source of truth in §3.
4. CSV export previously omitted cybersecurity/clinical rows — fixed.
5. Stale FDA cybersecurity citation (2023 guidance) — corrected to the actual current 27 Jun 2025 final guidance.

