## §6 — Verification Status (restructured, matching the ClinicalCompass D-001 pattern)

**Not yet deep-verified:**
- Every rule-provenance tag (`REG`/`STD`/`GUID`/`DRAFT`/`ED`) was self-assigned during this build, not independently checked against primary sources clause-by-clause.
- The 8 critical gates' mapping to specific criteria (e.g. Gate 5 → cybersecurity SBOM criterion only) is a deliberate simplification — one representative criterion per gate, not a multi-criterion aggregate. Whether that's the right level of rigor should be independently assessed.
- WCAG contrast ratios on the new indigo accent (`#5b47e0`) against light/dark backgrounds — not measured with an actual contrast checker.

**Known deferred gaps** (see §4 — repeated here for the verification-log record): automated test suite, build hash, full AI taxonomy, temporal phase matrix, stale companion docs.

**Fastest-moving citations to re-check regardless of ship date:**
- AI Act Annex III deadline (2 Dec 2027) / Annex I deadline (2 Aug 2028) — Digital Omnibus, could shift again.
- EN 18286:2026 OJEU citation status — published by CEN-CENELEC but not yet cited in the Official Journal as of this build; presumption of conformity depends on that citation happening.
- FDA cybersecurity guidance — just corrected once already (2023 → Jun 2025); confirm no newer version has superseded it by port date.
- IEC 63450 / IEC 63521 — both still under development; confirm no publication has occurred.
- ISO/TS 24971-2 LLM/generative-AI exclusion clause — re-verify the tool's paraphrase of the exclusion against the actual published scope clause, not just the existence of an exclusion.

