## §7 — Open Questions Before Coding

1. Confirm repo remote/local path (§0 proposed values, not yet confirmed).
2. Should the companion spec/verification-protocol docs be regenerated before or after the repo port? (Recommend: after — port first, then regenerate docs against the ported, tested state rather than the pre-port HTML.)
3. Review cadence: adopt the same quarterly cycle as CyberCompass/RegCompass (first due 2026-11-18), or start LifecycleCompass's own clock from port date?
4. Test framework choice (Jest, or whatever the other Compass repos already standardized on, if any).
5. Should independent regulatory review happen against the current single-file HTML before port, or against the ported+tested repo version? (Recommend: against the ported version, so the reviewer isn't reviewing something about to change under them.)
6. Confirm the exact GitHub-side mechanism for enforcing §5a (push restriction to a single named account vs. required commit-signature verification vs. both) — decide before the first commit, not after.

